mb|1C|MB|?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|You can overcall at the one level with as little as 8 points and when you can lay claim to the spade suit you should. Just using those two factors, some might say I should bid 1@S. Unfortunately, because I have such a weak hand and weak suit, I think pass is better.|
PG| ***** 1 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at| Had my diamond honors been in my spade suit I would have overcalled one spade. So remember that part of hand evaluation has to do with, not only how many points you have, but where they are located.|
PG| ***** 2 ***** |


mb|P|mb|1H|mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I agree with pass by North. In order to overcall 2@D, North should either have 6+ diamonds or better diamonds--3 honors or two honors and a couple of intermediates.|
PG| ***** 3 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|1S|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Both 1@S or 2@S are possible bids with the EAST hand. I actually like 2@S slightly better, particularly because the heart honors fit well with partner, but 1@S is possible as well. 2@S here is a jump shift, establishing a game force. which is why it is slightly aggressive. It is not  |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=reverses,Reverses^*N|CP||FP||at|. That makes 2@S bid more aggressive while 1@S is slightly conservative. Were it a legal, ^*B1.75 Spades^*n bid would be perfect.|

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 4 ***** |


mb|P|mb|2C|mb|P3C|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|A good 3@C bid. 4@C too strong so 3@C is best you can do.|
PG| ***** 5 ***** |


