AT|
^*BEast: ^*NSo we missed game?|
PG| ***** 21 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^^
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Well yes and no. 5@C makes because the spade finesse works.|
PG| ***** 22 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|In Match Points, 50% games are even money in terms of how well you do on the deal. However, in IMPs, you should be in a 50% game non-vulnerable and a 40% game vulnerable.|
PG| ***** 23 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I have a lesson on the differences between Match Point and IMP tactics which some of you might find interesting on my website. Please click the blue hyperlink. |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=scoring,SCORING^*N|CP||FP||
PG| ***** 24 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Had you bid 2@S rather than 1@S, you would have gotten to game. Let's look at East's |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=bergenstartingpoints,Bergen Starting Points^*N|CP||FP||at| to decide if 2@S was reasonable. East hand has 16 HCP, plus 2 length points, and 2 quality suit points. Normally you deduct one for Qx of hearts but once partner bids 1@H you don't do that. So East hand has at least 20 point. |

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 25 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|It is certainly enough to bid 2@S and force to game if you were in an aggressive mood. With East bidding 2@S West should bid 3@C. Then East should bid 3@D, which is a stopper ask. With a diamond stopper, East would bid 3N. Now West without a diamond stopper has a problem as to whether to bid 4@C or 5@C. It is tough to know and since game is on a finesse, either bid would be fine.|
PG| ***** 26 ***** |


