UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|They definitely should not be in slam as both major suit queens have to be onside for slam to make. Just because you make slam does not mean you should bid it. It is a 25% slam, depending on 2 finesses. You do not want to bid a 25% slam.|
PG| ***** 68 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|And this is why those double dummy analyzers can be very misleading. They will say you can make 6NT which is true. But that doesn't mean you should bid it. You need to analyze the odds of making a contract. Just because it makes does not mean you should bid it.|
PG| ***** 69 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|And conversely, just because a contract goes down due to some bad luck does not mean you should not be there. EW should still not be in slam. You want to only bid small slams that are more than 50%. And grand slams should only be bid if you can count 13 tricks..|
PG| ***** 70 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Again, see my lesson on Match Point and IMP tactics |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=scoring, SCORING^*N|CP||FP||
PG| ***** 71 ***** |


