mb|1C|mb|P?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Many players would bid 2N with my hand showing a balanced 11-12, invitational to bid 3N. However, that is not my favorite bid because it takes up a lot of room admittedly with 4-3-3-3 distribution it is still tempting. Nevertheless, I am going to bid 2@C |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=invertedminors,Inverted Minors^*N|CP||FP||at| raise showing 10+ points and 4+ clubs|
PG| ***** 73 ***** |


mb|2C|mb|P?|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Let me discuss a bid for North that most players would not think of. North has 16 HCP, 1 length point, 2 quality suit points, 2 points for the singleton, and 1 point for the side 4+ card heart suit once a fit is established for 22. slam is very likely, especially with all suits controlled.|
PG| ***** 74 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|One choice that most players would not think of is 3@S a |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=splinters,Splinter^*N|CP||FP||at| bid showing a singleton spade and agreeing on clubs as trumps.|
PG| ***** 75 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|The other is,  |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=kickback,Kickback RKCB^*N|CP||FP||at|. That is a bid I play. Please click the blue hyperlink to learn more about it. If You play |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=kickback,Kickback RKCB^*N|CP||FP||at| the bid is the suit just above trumps. 4@D is RKCB for clubs, 4@H is RKCB for diamonds, 4@S is RKCB for hearts, and 4N is RKCB for spades.|
PG| ***** 76 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|So on this hand, since North has all suits controlled and enough points for slam should bid 4@D as RKCB.|
PG| ***** 77 ***** |


mb|4D|mb|P|mb|4H|an|0 or 3|
PG| ***** 78 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|In response to RKCB I play 0314 system (which is what I recommend although many play 1430). 4@H = 0 or 3, 4@S = 1 or 4, 4N = 2 keys no trump Queen, and 5@C = 2 keys with trump Queen.|
PG| ***** 79 ***** |


mb|P|mb|6C|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|6@C is the correct bid.|
