UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|This hand is a useful illustration of two important bidding principles. The most important is Bergen Hand Evaluation, which I always emphasize as the most important thing you can learn to improve your bidding--better than any convention. That allowed North to figure out how strong her hand was and that slam was likely if we had enough key cards.|
PG| ***** 95 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|The second, occasionally useful principle, was using Kickback RKCB. That really helps with minor suit slams because it keeps you low enough to remain in 5 of the minor if you don't have enough key cards.|
PG| ***** 96 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|If you play 4N as RKCB and are in a minor suit, then you usually go past 5 of your minor and are forced to bid slam even though you lack enough key cards. Kickback fixes that problem.|
PG| ***** 97 ***** |


